From 8979fea523711dcc48ccfe0e900ed0b9d663d5c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:32:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] TEACH-3AXES: teach points for MOutShuttle1 / MOutShuttle2 /
 MCCDY (W906 extension, not golden) + their Teach interlock

EastSun 1001: the three axes are enabled PCIE-1203 axes with no teach points. Six TECH_PARA rows appended at the very
end of the registry (before golden :993, so every golden TechPara index / button Tag is unchanged), registered only
when IO_CARD_TYPE==PCI1203_IO (other machines' teach.ini get no new keys):
  [MOutShuttle1] setEditOutSht1Left / setEditOutSht1Right -> Tech.iOutShuttle1Left / 1Right (Prod.OutSHT[0])
  [MOutShuttle2] setEditOutSht2Left / setEditOutSht2Right -> Tech.iOutShuttle2Left / 2Right (Prod.OutSHT[1])
  [MCCDY]        setEditCCDYSite1x1 / setEditCCDYCal1x1   -> Tech.iCCDYSite1x1 / Tech.iCalY1x1
Buttons btnSet*/btnGo* (new names, not in golden's dfm), handlers SetButton140Click / GoButton140Click.

- tools/gen_teach_registry.py: EXT_ROWS (one definition) emitted before golden :993; forms/fTeachRegistry.cpp
  re-spliced from a fresh run (golden part byte-identical).
- tools/gen_teach_editlist.py: golden prefix still compared row by row with golden (312 / 624 unchanged); the tail
  must equal EXT_ROWS; extension buttons must not be golden dfm names, not Motor*, keys not colliding with a golden
  row of the same section, not elTeach widgets. WebTeachButtons.gen.inc / FileRW/Teach.gen.inc regenerated;
  --check passes.
- forms/fTeach.cpp: IsCanQuickJogMove's last `return true` (same line) -> W906_Teach3AxesHomeOk: MOutShuttle1/2 need
  MTestZ1, MTestZ2, In/Out Arm Z at home (golden In Shuttle branch shape); MCCDY needs MTestZ1, MTestZ2 (golden
  Index Y branch shape); same W906_TeachHomeLed predicate (Enable=0 non-1203 axes not checked); other axes unchanged.
- tests: test_web_motor_access (312+6 rows; PCI1203_IO registry resolves the six buttons, own rows, not quirks);
  test_gali_route_engine part 16 (the real IsCanQuickJogMove for the three axes).

First boot on the machine writes the six keys into teach.ini (golden CheckAndReadIniData, value = current Tech, 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
